' --- Diagrama: comparação Caminho A (HTTP) vs Caminho B (PowerShell) ---
@startuml
title Caminhos de análise dinâmica — comparação A vs B
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

left to right direction

package "Caminho A — VM Agent HTTP" #E3F2FD {
  [Frontend / API] as A_FE
  [VM Orchestrator\nvm_orchestrator.py] as A_VMO
  [Driver hyperv\nou proxmox] as A_DRV
  [Hyper-V VM] as A_VM
  [vm-agent\nMinimal API] as A_AGENT
}

package "Caminho B — PowerShell Hyper-V" #FFF9C4 {
  [WPF Desktop] as B_WPF
  [04-Run-Sample.ps1\n+ fases RunSample] as B_PS
  [Hyper-V VM] as B_VM
  [Run-MalwareAnalysis.ps1\n+ Sysmon] as B_GUEST
}

' *Caminho A: orquestrador no backend via HTTP*
A_FE --> A_VMO : POST /api/analysis
A_VMO --> A_DRV
A_DRV --> A_VM : restore snapshot\nstart / stop
A_DRV --> A_AGENT : HTTP REST\nupload · run · report
A_AGENT --> A_VM

' *Caminho B: orquestração local WPF + PsDirect*
B_WPF --> B_PS : orquestração local
B_PS --> B_VM : restore snapshot\nCopy-VMFile / PsDirect
B_PS --> B_GUEST : credenciais guest
B_GUEST --> B_VM

note bottom of A_AGENT
  Telemetria básica
  (processo, stdout/stderr)
  Orquestrador: backend
end note

note bottom of B_GUEST
  Telemetria completa
  (ficheiros, registry, rede)
  Orquestrador: WPF / scripts
end note

note as N1
  **Independentes** — HTTP vs PsDirect.
  Ambos usam switch Internal e snapshot CleanState.
  O driver hyperv **não** invoca 04-Run-Sample.ps1.
end note

@enduml
